version: "2.0"
description: >-
  packages/gnomon-mods - the first-party Gnomon mods (spec §12.1). They run on
  the same mod-abi:v1 and the same `mod` sandbox profile as any other mod;
  first-party is a trust tier derived from the packageHash pinned in the
  kernel's FIRST_PARTY_PACKAGE_HASHES (packages/gnomon/src/kernel/manifest/install.ts),
  never a wider ABI. Files are LF-pinned (.gitattributes) so the hash is the
  same on every OS.

components:
  workshop-mod:
    description: >-
      #workshop-mod (spec §11.6, G-WSP-01; §19.1 M1.11 slice 3) -
      packages/gnomon-mods/workshop: one view `workshop.strip` (slot sidebar,
      append) with two zones, needs you (one cap per pending card, labelled
      by the card kind) and working (one cap per session: hat = work type,
      filled = Claude, outlined = local, tone hue-<0..5> = project
      (HUES = 6, the feed's projectHue), violet only for a KNOT; bob while
      turn.partial streams, still otherwise, `working` text pose under
      reduced motion). S5: every cap is a Text whose `text` is the accessible
      form and whose `cap` is the closed contracts shape {shape tall|wide|
      floppy, hue, filled, state needs|working|idle|knot, label} (needs caps
      carry their session's hue and a `◆ / ✕ / ! / ?` + kind label); the GUI
      draws the hat and the Layout places the strip. model.mjs is a pure reducer
      + render (sessions and cards bounded at 256 each); index.mjs speaks
      mod-abi:v1 directly (no SDK import, so the pinned packageHash never
      depends on an SDK build) and echoes MOD_ABI_ID. State comes ONLY from
      the host's projected kernel-event feed (#mod-host feed.ts, granted by
      the log.read capability), primed at every start with the state in force
      (#mod-host feedBacklog: live sessions, pending cards, paused mods), so a
      Workshop started after a session opened still counts it; a host-initiated fixture render may replay
      input.fixtureEvents, a relayed render never can. Declared effects:
      none beyond idle read; tier first-party; installs with
      `gnomon mod install packages/gnomon-mods/workshop` + the root-key card.
      Fixtures strip.json / strip-reduced.json with golden renders
      (test/workshop-mod.test.ts, every OS).
      1.1.1 (Dimensions S1.2): echoes the moved modAbiId; no behaviour change;
      re-pinned in FIRST_PARTY_PACKAGE_HASHES.
    tags: [mods, first-party, M1.11]
    oracles: [G-WSP-01]

  ledger-mod:
    description: >-
      #ledger-mod - packages/gnomon-mods/ledger, the context and budget
      meter (mod #1 of the mods arc). Two views: `ledger.strip` (slot
      composer.footer, append) - one line for the focused session (relay
      input {hsid}, display only) or all sessions, `182k in · 9k out · 71%
      cache · $0.42 · ⇣ 2 compactions (190k → 41k)` (in = fresh + cache
      reads + cache writes; cache = the share read from cache; a local
      session shows its token total), the budget meter (the over-permit row
      `n of m`, else the highest budget.ladder rung `n of 100%`) and the
      alarms (breaker open, permit denied); `ledger.sheet` (slot sidebar,
      append) - a Table row per session plus the total, meter and alarms.
      Tones: quiet; warn (amber) at a rung >= 75% or an over-permit row;
      deny (vermilion) on a breaker or a denied permit; hue-<0..7> ONLY on
      the cap glyph, never as text. Reduced motion renders the meter as Text
      (no Progress fill at all). kit:v1 blocks only (Box, Text, Table,
      Progress). model.mjs is a pure reducer + render (MAX_SESSIONS 256,
      MAX_DIMENSIONS 32, every number re-clamped by count(), unknown kinds
      ignored); index.mjs is the #workshop-mod stdio loop verbatim but for
      the two views (no SDK import, echoes MOD_ABI_ID). State comes ONLY from
      the #mod-host feed projection v2 (numbers only, granted by log.read);
      a relayed render never replays fixtureEvents. requires log.read and
      log.read:usage (Aegis M1: the usage rows reach only that grant),
      egress none, no tools or commands; tier first-party (packageHash pinned in FIRST_PARTY_PACKAGE_HASHES). Fixtures strip, strip-reduced,
      over-budget, breaker, compacted with golden renders
      (test/ledger-mod.test.ts, light and dark); goldens regenerate with
      `npm run repin:first-party` in packages/gnomon
      (packages/gnomon/scripts/repin-first-party.mjs, which renders the
      Workshop, Ledger and Paradigm Context goldens from their pure models).
      1.1.1 (Dimensions S1.2): echoes the moved modAbiId; no behaviour change;
      re-pinned in FIRST_PARTY_PACKAGE_HASHES.
    tags: [mods, first-party]
  paradigm-context-mod:
    description: >-
      #paradigm-context-mod - packages/gnomon-mods/paradigm-context, Paradigm
      Context (mod #2 of the mods arc). One view `paradigm-context.sheet`
      (slot sidebar, append), read-only (no Button, no command, no tool): a
      head with the project swatch (tone hue-<0..7> on the ● mark only, which
      the GUI draws as the project's ■; the name in ink), a stale line (warn)
      when the newest decision or lore entry is > STALE_DAYS (14) older than
      the slice's `at`; a project with no open tasks, decisions or lore
      shows ONE quiet line (EMPTY_LINE 'nothing yet: no tasks, decisions or
      lore') instead of the zones; otherwise three zones, each headed by a row: the zone name
      (Text tone head, the label style) and its {n, of} count as quiet meta
      (`tasks` `n of m open · k high`, `decisions` `n of m`, `lore` `n of m`;
      1.1.1, 2026-10-23) - each item a row with a FIXED type prefix
      (`task` / `task ▲` for high, `decision`, `lore <type>`), the id (a
      decision's date its own word after it, so the GUI truncates the id and
      never the date), then the title “quoted” (inner curly quotes flattened), every
      part tone quiet, so a repo title never supplies a status glyph (Aegis
      L2) - then the symbols touched as chips (tone chip,
      mono ink, never a hue), and a skipped line (malformed / refused /
      secret counts). Titles cut to 80 code points. Its ONLY input is the
      host-composed `input.paradigm` (#mod-host K1 paradigm-slice:v1 of the
      focused LIVE session's repo, joined server-side from {focus:{hsid}},
      K3); model.mjs re-validates and bounds it (ids, dates, tokens, symbol
      shape, counts). requires paradigm.read:summary only (no log.read, so
      no feed), egress none (refused with that capability). index.mjs is the
      #ledger-mod stdio loop minus the feed (no SDK import, echoes
      MOD_ABI_ID). Fixtures empty, full, full-dark, stale, unfocused with
      goldens (test/paradigm-context-mod.test.ts, light and dark);
      regenerate with `npm run repin:first-party`; tier first-party once
      pinned in FIRST_PARTY_PACKAGE_HASHES (1.1.1 sha256:22bab5bf…, repinned 2026-10-23 for the fitted zone heads and the one-line empty state).
      1.1.2 (Dimensions S1.2): echoes the moved modAbiId; no behaviour change;
      re-pinned in FIRST_PARTY_PACKAGE_HASHES (sha256:bd25b714…, superseding the
      1.1.1 pin named above).
    tags: [mods, first-party]
  neurons-mod:
    description: >-
      #neurons-mod - packages/gnomon-mods/neurons-brain (the Desk, TD-2026-10-20-812
      slice S2), mod name `neurons-brain`, because `neurons` is a kernel
      namespace token (the §9.1 `neurons.event` kind) and the validator refuses
      it as a mod name. View-less, with no process of its own (no index.mjs; the
      validator needs none). It declares one provides.mcp server `gnomon-neurons-brain`
      (generic default `neurons mcp`, a placeholder that is not absolute, so it
      fails closed until the user sets an absolute command through the
      per-user override; config {command, args, env [NEURONS_VAULT], the
      upstream server's own variable}; no personal path is committed), three
      offers (search-the-brain diverge → neuron_search, capture-a-learning
      synthesize → source_note, capture-a-decision commit → neuron_write; each
      offer's contextIn comes from CONTEXT_SOURCES, and the two capture
      restraints, like the playbook, require showing the exact text and waiting
      for the human to confirm or edit it, flagging fetched, tool-output or
      unverified content), and one skill, skills/neurons-desk/SKILL.md, a
      playbook that falls back to plain suggestions outside Gnomon. Every
      ```offer example in it resolves to a declared offer (tested). requires egress none,
      no capability. Fixtures are model replies with one ```offer block, and
      their goldens come from scripts/offer-golden.mjs (offerBlockOf plus the
      manifest's offer-spec), with one undeclared-kind negative. Tier
      first-party (packageHash pinned in FIRST_PARTY_PACKAGE_HASHES); tested
      in test/neurons-mod.test.ts.
    tags: [mods, first-party, desk]
    oracles: [G-DSK-06, G-DSK-07, G-DSK-08]
  constellation-mod:
    description: >-
      #constellation-mod - packages/gnomon-mods/constellation (the Desk,
      TD-2026-10-20-812 slice S2). View-less, with no process of its own. It
      declares one provides.mcp server `gnomon-constellation` (placeholder
      default `constellation-mcp`, never launched: it is not absolute, so it
      fails closed until the user sets an absolute node and
      `<checkout>/mcp/server.ts` through the per-user override; config
      {command, args, env [CONSTELLATION_NO_AUTOSTART]}), two offers
      (map-the-idea diverge → apply, contextIn [recent-messages];
      summarize-the-session synthesize → summarize; the automation offer is
      deferred to O2 behind a confirmation and a disabled save, Aegis H1), and
      one skill, skills/constellation-desk/SKILL.md, a playbook that falls back
      to plain suggestions outside Gnomon. requires egress none, no capability.
      The L3 "sky" world is not declared yet, because manifest:v1 has no world
      field. Offer fixtures plus goldens include a two-blocks negative. Tier
      first-party (packageHash pinned); tested in
      test/constellation-mod.test.ts.
    tags: [mods, first-party, desk]
    oracles: [G-DSK-06, G-DSK-07, G-DSK-08]
  dimension-mod:
    description: >-
      #dimension-mod (spec §12.7; S1.3 P2, S1.4 P3; first-party) -
      packages/gnomon-mods/dimension, id gnomon.dimension: the ONE writer of
      dimension rows. Seven commands, each declaring effects (dim.open,
      dim.attach, dim.op, dim.close, dim.grant read+write; dim.select,
      dim.check read); the four modns.gnomon.dimension.* kinds and the two
      auxiliary ones (grant, draw.refused); tools dim-view (read) and dim-draw
      (read, write) for an attached session's agent (S1.4: see below); no view, keybinding,
      offer, capability or egress. model.mjs is pure: actorOf (a human only
      for a host stamp with surface gui and no agent), apply(state, ops,
      actor) (the one entry: validateDimOps, rows built from its accepted
      copies), titleProblem, grantDefault, readArgs (closed arg shapes, read
      field by field, never spread), rowProblem and the keyframe codec.
      index.mjs is the stdio loop plus a mod-to-host request helper. Every
      command checks the stamp, the args, the attached session and the repo
      before any append; the 512-dimension cap, the 16-session attach cap
      and the row-size check run before the append; mod state and the fold
      move only after a seq. State: `dims`, `idx:<ulid>` {repo, firstSeq,
      lastSeq, title, log}, `kfs`, and keyframes `kf:<ulid>` + chunks of at
      most 60 KiB for the 4 most recent dimensions (at close and every 256
      ops, skipped above 256 KiB, 640 KiB in all), each bound to its log id.
      The LOG is the truth and the index a hint: a cold open verifies the
      keyframe (sum, dimHash, log id), then pages log.read for the four
      kinds from its seq to the log head, one foldDim per page, and heals
      the index; a dimension with rows but no index is adopted from its first
      start row and that row's repo scope; entries of another log are pruned
      once (`log` key); a failed append drops the in-memory fold. apply
      measures the caller's ops (16 KiB, 4,096 values, depth 32) BEFORE the
      validator reads them. dim-shape.mjs is GENERATED from
      #contract-dim-shape by packages/gnomon/scripts/build-dimension-mod.mjs
      and compared with a fresh build by a test. Tier first-party
      (packageHash pinned). 1.0.1 (S1.4 P0): dim-shape.mjs rebuilt from the
      tightened contract (scan cap, wider strip set, view re-validation,
      DIM_AUX_KINDS, the write-grant fold) and grantDefault now reads the
      published dimGrantDefault; no command, tool, kind or state key changes.
      The 1.0.0 pin is replaced and RETIRED (RETIRED_FIRST_PARTY_PINS in
      #manifest-loader), not superseded. An install already pinned at 1.0.0
      keeps loading first-party, because loadMod takes the tier from that
      install's signed grant.trust row, until the person approves the Update
      card; 1.0.0 can no longer be staged, approved from an old card or
      rolled back to (test/retired-pins.test.ts). Tested in test/dimension-mod.test.ts (rules,
      caps, keyframes, isolation) and test/dimension-relay.test.ts (the
      relay table per caller class over real connections, a mod's own
      log.read, first-party identity). 1.1.0 (S1.4 P3, never shipped before
      this pass): dim.grant{dim, write} for a person on the GUI, target = the
      attached focus hsid the host joins (a client hsid is stripped; a session
      that is not live cannot be granted), grant rows folded through the
      shared foldDimGrants on every log page, keyframe v2 carrying the grant
      map and the op-id memo as lists (v1 ignored); dim.open and dim.grant
      answer the effective map (M9), attach writes no grant (M10).
      dim.select (memory only), dim.check {seq, hash} with no write (the page's
      hash point after an agent turn), hash on dim.op. Tools: toolActorOf
      (whole agent stamp, turn of the same hsid), readToolInput (closed
      shape), dim-view (opens default from dim.open and dim.attach, since,
      limit, own selection, strokes as count+box), dim-draw (order of checks,
      resolveSugar, ONE validation, packRows into 4 rows inside 64 KiB less a
      count-row reserve, oid = sha256(hsid,0,dim,0,opId)[0:16] on the row,
      memo of 256 oids and 32 answers, `turns` budget of 64 ops charged
      BEFORE the first row and never refunded, grant re-read between rows,
      count row of closed keys at most 8 per hsid and turn). appendTool lets
      a tool append only op and draw.refused (M4). cancel is honoured between
      log pages and rows (M3); an APPEND_BUDGET refusal keeps the fold
      (append-busy, A4). PLAYBOOK.md is the long form of the agent rules.
      Review fixes (S1.4 P3): a tool never adopts (an unindexed dim is
      dim-unknown before any log read); ops of rows definitely not written
      are refunded, a failed append never is; dimHash cached per fold (WeakMap);
      a cold repeat says inputUnknown; NEW_KEY_FIX for an undefined new:<key>;
      the op-id input is canonical JSON and measured first; read-only calls
      never saveIdx; an agent may add inside another hand's frame. Open: a
      resumed session's turn numbers restart at 1 (I-3).
      State keys added: opens, turns. Tested in test/dimension-tools.test.ts
      (G-DDL-03, G-DDL-09, A8, M3, M4, M8, M9, A4 with a real-window clock,
      G-MOD-20) and test/dimension-kinds.test.ts (all six kinds refused for
      every other writer).
    tags: [mods, first-party, dimensions]
    oracles: [G-DDL-01, G-DDL-03, G-DDL-09, G-MOD-16, G-MOD-17, G-MOD-18, G-MOD-20]
